{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1720","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1720","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1720\",\"parent_revision\":\"211a0a51ad8fb3b996d125c3dcee154d6f19531bda6011eea57cdbab9379e006\",\"root_revision\":\"211a0a51ad8fb3b996d125c3dcee154d6f19531bda6011eea57cdbab9379e006\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: fix: Invented truncation limits in backlog MCP server silently drop content\\nDate: 2026-04-12\\nGoal: Remove two invented [:N] slices in server.py that silently drop operator-visible content, replacing them with full-content pass-through (or explicit truncation markers with length metadata if a downstream bound is unavoidable).\\nConditions:\\n1. Both bug locations confirmed: server.py:4288 (content[:4096]) and server.py:4355 (stdout_text[:200]) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker VERIFIED via Read tool\\n2. Both truncations emit no warning, no flag, no character count | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker VERIFIED via code inspection lines 4280-4310, 4350-4365\\n3. Fix scope is narrow \u2014 two targeted slice replacements | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: fact-checker VERIFIED, impact-analyst confirmed\\n4. Whether set_item_complete storage layer imposes size constraint on content | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 SQLite result TEXT column is unbounded; no downstream constraint justifies the 4096 limit\\n5. Whether any downstream consumer enforces a size limit | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: impact-analyst \u2014 dispatch_item_status path (line 4099) passes result untruncated; SQLite error TEXT also unbounded; both paths are inconsistent with the truncated