y` | Role: test | Connection: tests `set_item_complete` but with short payloads only; missing >4096 round-trip test | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` | Role: test | Connection: end-to-end dispatch spawn test; does not exercise large payload or non-JSON spawn error paths | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: line 173 contains `[:200]` slice in bash result-reading example \u2014 teaches truncation pattern | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: documents `set_item_complete` signature; no size claim | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` | Role: ci | Connection: runs pytest suite; will automatically cover new regression tests | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 two active truncation bug sites; silent data loss on every large-payload dispatch completion and every spawn failure with verbose output\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_state.py` \u2014 no regression test for the core fix acceptance criterion (>4096-char round-trip); fix can silently regress without it\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` \u2014 non-JSON spawn error path has zero test coverage\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - behavioral: result file content beyond 4096 chars is silently dropped from the stored record\\n  - verification: neither truncation site has a test asserting the bug or protecting against regression\\n  - documentation: `work-milestone/SKILL.md` line 173 models the truncation anti-pattern in agent-facing instructions\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - Third truncation site discovered in `skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md:173` (not mentioned in original item description) \u2014 a `[:200]` slice in a bash code example that reads result_file content. This is an AI-facing instruction that can propagate the anti-pattern. Planning scope should include updating this example.\\n  - Two distinct completion code paths exist (`_poll_until_done` vs `dispatch_item_status`): only the internal polling path has the bug. The external MCP tool path is already correct. This asymmetry should be documented and tested.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n- Dispatch completion and spawn-error paths either return full content or, if a downstream consumer enforces a bound, emit an explicit truncation marker with the original length.\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" rule is satisfied \u2014 grep for `\\\\[:\\\\d+\\\\]` in backlog_core shows no silent truncation on operator-visible output.\\n- Regression test asserts that a >4096-character completion payload round-trips intact.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **invented truncation limits in backlog mcp server silently drop content** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Verified code audit 2026-04-12 \u2014 .tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-ux-analysis-verified.md (c7)\\n- **Priority**: P0\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-12\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-12)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n**Truncation 1 \u2014 completion payload (`server.py:4288`)**\\n\\n1. Start the development-harness MCP server.\\n2. Using the `dispatch_spawn` or equivalent tool, dispatch a task whose result file will exceed 4096 characters (e.g., a task that writes a long JSON summary to its result file).\\n3. Wait for the task to complete via `_poll_until_done`.\\n4. Call `dispatch_item_status` or `dispatch_wave_status` and inspect the `result` field of the completed item.\\n5. Observe: the returned `result` string ends at 4096 characters; content beyond that boundary is absent with no warning, no truncation flag, and no character count.\\n\\n**Truncation 2 \u2014 spawn error message (`server.py:4355`)**\\n\\n1. Trigger a spawn failure in which `spawn.py` writes more than 200 characters of non-JSON output to stdout (e.g., a Python traceback).\\n2. Observe the error message returned in the MCP tool `warnings` list or stored in the SQLite `error` column.\\n3. Observe: the error string ends at 200 characters; the remainder of stdout is absent with no indication that content was dropped.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nEffort: Small\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Blocks**: Any operator or agent that reads `dispatch_wave_status` or `dispatch_item_status` results to audit or debug dispatch work \u2014 results are silently incomplete for payloads > 4096 characters.\\n- **Blocks**: Debugging spawn failures where `spawn.py` produces verbose non-JSON output \u2014 the real error is hidden past character 200.\\n- **Bottleneck**: Post-dispatch result inspection and spawn-failure root-cause analysis both depend on data that is being silently dropped at the storage layer.\\n- **Recurring pattern**: The same anti-pattern appears in `skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md:173` (`d.get('result','')[:200]`), propagating the behaviour into agent-generated code.\\n- **Test gap**: Zero tests cover the >4096-character completion round-trip path or the non-JSON spawn error path, so neither truncation is caught by CI.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen an orchestrator marks a dispatch item complete with any length of result payload, the full payload is stored in the SQLite `result TEXT` column and returned unmodified by `dispatch_wave_status` and `dispatch_item_status`.\\n\\nWhen `spawn.py` returns non-JSON stdout, the complete stdout text is included in the error message surfaced to the operator and stored in the SQLite `error TEXT` column.\\n\\nIf any downstream consumer must impose a size bound, it does so explicitly: it states that the content is truncated, reports the original length, and provides a mechanism (e.g., `--offset`/`--limit` parameters) to access the remaining content. Neither the storage layer nor the internal polling path imposes a bound, because the SQLite `result TEXT` and `error TEXT` columns are unbounded.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -n '\\\\[:[0-9]' plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` returns no matches on `content`, `result`, `stdout_text`, `stderr_text`, or `error_msg` variables in operator-visible output paths.\\n2. A pytest test in `test_dispatch_state.py` asserts that a string of > 4096 characters stored via `set_item_complete` is retrieved intact (character-for-character) from SQLite.\\n3. A pytest test covers the non-JSON spawn error path and asserts that the full `stdout_text` (> 200 characters) appears in the stored error record and in the tool response.\\n4. Both new tests pass under `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_state.py plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py`.\\n5. `skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` line 173 no longer contains a `[:N]` slice on a result variable in its code example.\\n6. The `dispatch_wave_status` tool response for a completed item with a > 4096-character result returns the full result string.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Rule | `/home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u00a7\\\"No Invented Limits\\\" \u2014 the policy these truncations violate |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` lines 4288, 4355 \u2014 the two bug sites |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/dispatch_state.py::DispatchStateManager.set_item_complete` \u2014 storage layer; no size constraint |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_state.py::TestSetItemComplete` \u2014 existing tests to extend |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` line 173 \u2014 third truncation instance in agent instructions |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n| File | Role | Action needed |\\n|------|------|---------------|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` line 4288 | Bug site 1 \u2014 `_poll_until_done` passes `content[:4096]` to `set_item_complete` | Remove `[:4096]` slice |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` line 4355 | Bug site 2 \u2014 `_run_spawn_item` builds error message with `stdout_text[:200]` | Remove `[:200]` slice |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_state.py` | Unit tests for `set_item_complete`; only short payloads covered | Add >4096-char round-trip regression test |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_tools.py` | End-to-end dispatch tests; non-JSON spawn error path not covered | Add non-JSON spawn error path test |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md` line 173 | Agent instruction models `[:200]` slice on result read \u2014 propagates anti-pattern | Remove or replace `[:200]` slice in code example |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 both bug sites are self-contained call-site changes with no upstream prerequisite.\\n- Blocks: Any work that relies on accurate full-content dispatch completion records or complete spawn failure diagnostics. The `dispatch_wave_status` and `dispatch_item_status` result fields are inputs to downstream audit and debugging tooling.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 Two targeted slice removals in `server.py` (two characters removed per site), plus two new regression tests and one SKILL.md example update. No schema changes, no interface changes, no migration. The storage layer already accepts unbounded strings.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: DIVERGENT\\n**Design intent**: `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u00a7\\\"No Invented Limits\\\" requires: output full content by default; when pagination is needed, provide --offset/--limit; if shortened, state that it is truncated, report how many chars remain, and provide a way to access the rest. This applies to MCP tool responses, CLI output, JSON fields, and error messages.\\n**Divergence**: `server.py:4288` drops completion payload beyond 4096 characters with no warning, no character count, and no recovery path. `server.py:4355` drops spawn error output beyond 200 characters under the same conditions. Both are operator-debugging paths where the hidden content is most needed.\\n**Additional divergence**: `skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md:173` models the same truncation pattern in AI-facing code examples, propagating the anti-pattern to generated code.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: recurring-pattern\\n**Rationale**: The invented-truncation anti-pattern appears at minimum 3 times across this codebase: `server.py:4288` (`content[:4096]`), `server.py:4355` (`stdout_text[:200]`), and `skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md:173` (`d.get('result','')[:200]`). The same design assumption \u2014 \\\"add a slice to cap the length\\\" \u2014 recurs across code and AI-facing instructions without a guarding rule, indicating a systemic gap rather than an isolated mistake.\\n**Analysis Method**: 6-sigma (frequency measurement + root cause)\\n**Scenario Target**: Any operator-visible output path \u2192 full content or explicit truncation marker with length and access method\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\nFrequency: 3 confirmed instances of invented [:N] slice on operator-visible content within this plugin (server.py:4288, server.py:4355, SKILL.md:173).\\n\\nMeasurement:\\n- server.py:4288 \u2014 result payload capped at 4096 chars; SQLite result TEXT column is unbounded\\n- server.py:4355 \u2014 error message capped at 200 chars; SQLite error TEXT column is unbounded\\n- SKILL.md:173 \u2014 AI-facing code example uses [:200] on result file read\\n\\nRoot cause: The \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" rule in `.claude/CLAUDE.md` existed at the time these truncations were written but was not enforced at code review or by a linting rule. The absence of a grep-based quality gate (searching for `\\\\[:\\\\d+\\\\]` on operator-visible output paths) allows the pattern to recur.\\n\\nImprovement: Add a pre-commit or CI check that greps `backlog_core/` for `[:` slices on variables named `content`, `result`, `stdout`, `stderr`, `error_msg` and flags them for review. This converts a rule-of-thumb into an enforced constraint.\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nTwo call sites in `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` silently truncate content the consumer needs to read in full, violating the \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" rule in `.claude/CLAUDE.md`:\\n\\n- **`server.py:4288`** \u2014 `mgr.set_item_complete(milestone, wave_num, issue_num, content[:4096], item_cost)`. When an orchestrator marks a dispatch item complete, any payload beyond 4096 characters is silently dropped. The operator marking the item has no signal that the recorded completion payload is incomplete.\\n- **`server.py:4355`** \u2014 `error_msg = f\\\"spawn.py non-JSON output: {stdout_text[:200]}\\\"`. When `spawn.py` returns non-JSON, only the first 200 characters of stdout are surfaced. The operator debugging the spawn failure cannot see the actual error past character 200 \u2014 exactly when the full output is most needed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Dispatch completion records drop context beyond the 4096-character boundary with no warning emitted.\\n- Spawn-failure error messages hide the real cause past character 200.\\n- Both truncations are invisible to callers \u2014 there is no `truncated: true` flag, no character count, no pointer to the remaining content.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.tmp/scratch/reports/backlog-mcp-ux-analysis-verified.md` \u00a7c7 (verified via Grep in session)\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u2192 \\\"No Invented Limits\\\" section\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fact Check Summary\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Claim 1: `server.py:4288` contains `content[:4096]` truncation\\n**VERDICT**: VERIFIED\\n**Source**: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:4288\\n**Evidence**: `await asyncio.to_thread(mgr.set_item_complete, milestone, wave_num, issue_num, content[:4096], item_cost)`\\nThe content string is hardcoded to 4096-character limit before being passed to set_item_complete().\\n\\n### Claim 2: `server.py:4355` contains `stdout_text[:200]` truncation\\n**VERDICT**: VERIFIED\\n**Source**: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:4355\\n**Evidence**: `error_msg = f\\\"spawn.py non-JSON output: {stdout_text[:200]}\\\"`\\nThe stdout_text is hardcoded to 200-character limit in the error message string.\\n\\n### Claim 3: Neither truncation emits warnings/flags/counts/pointers\\n**VERDICT**: VERIFIED\\n**Evidence**: Code inspection lines 4280-4310 (Claim 1) and 4350-4365 (Claim 2) shows:\\n- No `truncated: true` flags\\n- No character count or remaining content indicators\\n- No warning/log messages indicating truncation occurred\\n- Silent data loss to downstream consumers\\n\\n### Claim 4: Evidence docu